# Tracer: ImgOfRealPlusImagScaled checks both rectangular coefficients in R.
# Before (incorrectly accepted):
# img(i + i) = 1
# img(0 + i * i) = i
# Former behavior: imaginary contributions inside either coefficient were ignored.
# Now: both real-coefficient premises are checked and retained.
forall a, b R:
    img(a + b * i) = b
    b = img(i * b + a)
img(i + i) = 2
# Boundary: either coefficient outside R prevents this identity from justifying the goal.
# Executable negatives: hcx_arithmetic_guards::false_operand_orders_and_complex_second_coefficients_reject.
